{
  "cross_references": [],
  "issue": {
    "body": "`URL` uses stdlib `urlsplit` to parse the string URL,\r\n\r\nhowever, it uses this code to recombine the host and port.\r\n\r\n```py\r\n            netloc = hostname                                                           \r\n            if port is not None:                                                        \r\n                netloc += f\":{port}\"  \r\n```\r\n\r\nConsider an IPv6 URL, like `http://[::1]:8080/`\r\n* urlsplit will strip the quare brackets and produce `::1` \r\n* manual concatenation will yield `::1:8080`\r\n* which is not a valid netloc",
    "closed_at": "2023-02-06T06:06:28Z",
    "created_at": "2022-11-02T05:19:06Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/1931",
    "labels": [
      "good first issue"
    ],
